From 90ebe2addf599dea6184b08ee68310de75822374 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lenin Mookiah <2639584+leninworld@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:18:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(daemon): gate workers on available memory on macOS
 (#2935)

On Darwin, os.freemem() counts only free and speculative pages. The kernel
keeps reclaimable file cache on the inactive queue, so an idle Mac reads as a
few percent "free" and the worker daemon defers almost every worker.

The memory gate now measures available memory on Darwin from vm_stat as
(free + speculative + inactive) x page size, clamped to totalmem, with the
page size read from vm_stat's own header (16 KiB on Apple Silicon). Purgeable
pages are not added because they already sit on other queues. Linux and
Windows keep os.freemem() unchanged.

vm_stat runs without a shell, with a 1 s timeout; concurrent checks share one
probe and results are cached for 5 s. If the probe fails the gate falls back
to os.freemem() and logs that once per daemon. Threshold defaults are not
changed.

Refs #2935

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
